mode: "100644"
text: "# Completion, Search & Volume — the three TikTok pillars\n\nThe three growth levers that are *distinctively* TikTok (more so than on Instagram). Pull these and\nthe FYP works in your favor.\n\n> Re-verify benchmarks quarterly (algorithm in flux through ~mid-2026); the principles are durable.\n\n## Pillar 1 — Completion + rewatch (the dominant signal)\n\nTikTok rewards one thing above all: **content people watch to the end, then watch again.**\n\n- **Aim ~70%+ completion** to have a real shot at going wide. That bar rose from ~50% in 2024, which\n  means **hooks and pacing have to be stronger than they used to be.**\n- **The first ~1 second** decides Phase 1. No intro, no logo, no slow build — open on the claim, the\n  stakes, or a striking visual. (→ `hook-writer`, `tiktok-script`.)\n- **Design for rewatch/loop** — the single most under-used lever. A seamless loop (the end flows into\n  the start), a fast line worth catching, a hidden detail, or density that needs two watches. A\n  rewatch counts the whole video again — it's the highest-leverage second you'll spend.\n- **Match length to completion, not to a number.** A 30-second video at 80% beats a 3-minute one at\n  40%. Shorter is usually safer for completion; go long only when the payoff sustains it.\n\nIf completion is low, nothing else matters — fix this first.\n\n## Pillar 2 — Search / SEO (the evergreen pillar, bigger than on IG)\n\nTikTok is a **search engine**, especially for younger users, and search is a *larger* growth channel\nhere than on Instagram. Most TikTok searches happen during exploration (people browsing for ideas),\nso search-optimized content gets discovered for **months**, independent of the FYP lottery.\n\n- **The triple mention:** put your **primary keyword in the spoken audio, the on-screen text, and the\n  caption** (front). TikTok transcribes audio and reads on-screen text — saying it + showing it +\n  writing it is the core ranking move. (→ `tiktok-script`, `hashtag-strategy`/`social-seo`.)\n- **Write captions like search queries** — the phrases people actually type (\"how to schedule posts\n  for free\"), not clever copy.\n- **Build keyword clusters** — multiple videos around a topic make TikTok see you as the answer for\n  that query. TikTok content also ranks on **Google**, a bonus discovery lane.\n- Hashtags are supporting keyword signals (treat as keywords, niche over `#fyp`) — not the main lever.\n\nSearch turns each video into a long-lived asset, not a 48-hour flash. This is how you grow *between*\nviral hits.\n\n## Pillar 3 — Volume of at-bats + read the patterns\n\nBecause every video is an independent, cheap **test**, growth is a numbers-and-learning game:\n\n- **Consistent at-bats.** A sustainable cadence (commonly ~**3–5×/week**, more if you can keep\n  quality) gives the algorithm more tests to find your winners and learns your style. Consistency\n  beats sporadic viral attempts; once-a-week-or-less reduces priority. **Match cadence to capacity**\n  (→ `content-calendar`) — quality-gated, because low-effort posts get buried.\n- **Judge by patterns, not single videos.** One flop is noise. Look across many videos: which\n  *hooks*, *topics*, or *formats* repeatedly land? That pattern is your signal — do more of it.\n  (→ `viral-reverse-engineering` to extract the mechanism.)\n- **The back-catalog keeps working** — videos can resurface weeks later, and search keeps old videos\n  discoverable. Every good post is a durable asset, so volume compounds.\n\nThe mindset: **produce → test → read the pattern → double down → prune.** Not \"make one perfect video\nand hope.\"\n"
